        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 73-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she was dyspnoeic with reduced oxygen saturation and increased sputum production. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and closely monitored with pulse oximetry and regular vital sign checks. Her condition improved satisfactorily and she was discharged in stable condition. Please continue maintenance bronchodilator therapy and ensure timely follow-up. Pulmonary rehabilitation referral is recommended. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
